{# Java typed-config subclass template — emits
src/main/java/org/prebid/server/spring/config/bidder/{Bidder}BidderConfigurationProperties.java

Only emitted when Rule 35 (config-properties subclass scaffolding) fired —
i.e., the source spec carries cross_language.go_specific_concerns[]:
hardcoded-config-as-anti-pattern, OR the source's adapter struct has fields
beyond `endpoint` (Kobler's `devEndpoint` is the canonical example).

Inputs:
  ctx.bidder_class_root  : str  — PascalCase (e.g., "Adverxo", "Kobler")
  ctx.typed_fields       : list[dict]  — per-field; each:
      java_name      : str  — Java field name (camelCase)
      java_type      : str  — fully-resolved Java type (String, Integer, List<String>, etc.)
      validation_annotations : list[str]|null  — e.g., ["@NotBlank", "@Min(0)"]
      notes          : str|null  — single-line // comment above the field
      default_value  : str|null  — RHS expression for the field initializer; null → no init
  ctx.javadoc_summary    : str|null  — class-level Javadoc summary

Lombok set: @Data + @NoArgsConstructor + @EqualsAndHashCode(callSuper = true).
@EqualsAndHashCode is mandatory because this class extends
BidderConfigurationProperties (which has its own equals/hashCode); without
callSuper=true Lombok emits a checkstyle warning and Jacoco branch-coverage
deficit.

Imports:
- jakarta.validation.constraints.* (only what's referenced via validation_annotations)
- lombok.{Data, EqualsAndHashCode, NoArgsConstructor}
- org.prebid.server.spring.config.bidder.model.BidderConfigurationProperties (the parent)

Caller is responsible for collecting the union of validation-annotation
imports across all typed_fields; this template assumes ctx.imports_extra
is the alphabetically-sorted list to emit.
#}
